          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "عیب ('eyb) — \"a flaw, a defect\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "تنها عیب این ماشین رنگ آن است. tanhâ 'eyb-e in mâshin rang-e ân ast. The only flaw of this car is its colour."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "'Eyb nadârad — never mind, it doesn't matter. Plural 'oyub, an Arabic broken plural."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "عیب ('eyb) is usually traced to Arabic 'ayb \"fault, blemish\"; in Persian it is a flaw in a thing or in a person."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
